Subject: appstream runner: offer only components the query names, unless an installed application or command has that name

The runner offers a component only when every word of the query occurs in
its name, id, package name or one of its keywords, not on a hit in its
summary or description alone. It stays silent only when an installed
application is named exactly what was typed, or an installed command is
(the shell runner's match for the query's first word), not on any
executable match another runner found, which includes the services
runner's fuzzy hits.
